#reason scripts/e2e-delegate/README.md The check table must name the guide flag and the panel guide check
#reason scripts/e2e-delegate/checks.mjs The e2e checks must fail a delegate run whose record has no guide
#reason scripts/e2e-delegate/verify.mjs The branch verify in the e2e run must pass --require-guide like the delegate does
#reason scripts/skill-test/fake-agent.mjs The fake delegate needs a valid guide, and a mode without one, to test the gate offline
#reason scripts/skill-test/run.mjs The no-guide fake must be selectable from the command line and documented in usage
#reason skills/lantern-delegate-complex/SKILL.md Keeps its description of what the heavy delegate records in step with the protocol
#reason skills/lantern-delegate/SKILL.md The orchestrator gate must require the guide and know which guides go back
#reason skills/lantern-delegate/protocol.md Delegates must write and record a guide so no PR ships without a reader's path through it
#reason skills/lantern-delegate/scripts/permissions.mjs An unattended delegate needs permission to edit its guide file
#reason skills/lantern-sync/SKILL.md The guide scratch path is now named, so the old note that it is open is wrong
#reason test/lantern-delegate-delivery-flow.test.ts Proves the offline run is red without a guide, and that verify carries the new flag
#story A delegate hands over its pull request
#step actor A delegate
#file skills/lantern-delegate/protocol.md
#step action writes a guide of the change
#step subject its pull request record
#file skills/lantern-delegate/scripts/permissions.mjs
#below interaction A reviewer reads the change as steps
#below consequence a record could ship with no guide => a record without a guide fails the gate
#story The orchestrator checks a handover
#step actor The orchestrator
#file skills/lantern-delegate/SKILL.md
#step action runs the gate with the guide flag
#step subject the delegate's branch
#file scripts/e2e-delegate/verify.mjs
#file scripts/e2e-delegate/checks.mjs
#file test/lantern-delegate-delivery-flow.test.ts
#below interaction Sends a weak guide back
#below consequence only the flow was read => the guide is read too
#guide Every delegate now writes a guide, and the delegate and orchestrator gates and the e2e checks require it.
#risk low Skill text, gate flags and a fake agent; no app code or record grammar changes.
#gstep careful What a delegate must write
#gwhy The protocol is the contract the delegates follow: it adds the guide file, the call flags and the rules for a good guide. The worked example must stay valid for the guide parser.
